import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for DaoismHub — what data the sites do and do not collect, cookies, server logs, email communication and contact."
>
  <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Last updated: October 10, 2026 &middot; Applies to daoismhub.com and data.daoismhub.com</p>

  <h2>1. Summary</h2>
  <p>
    DaoismHub is a static reference publication. We do not run user accounts, comments,
    newsletters or contact forms, and we do not operate advertising or analytics services.
    <strong>We collect no personal data through these websites.</strong> This policy
    documents that position in full, so that visitors understand exactly what happens
    when they browse.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Information we do not collect</h2>
  <p>Neither site collects, stores or processes:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Names, email addresses or other contact details (there is no registration);</li>
    <li>IP addresses, device fingerprints or browsing histories (there is no analytics);</li>
    <li>Behavioral, demographic or interest data (there is no advertising);</li>
    <li>Content you view beyond the standard operation of the hosting infrastructure.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Cookies and local storage</h2>
  <p>
    We do not set any cookies. The Data Registry's search function operates entirely in
    your browser: queries are matched against an index file and never leave your device,
    and no query history is stored by us.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Technical server logs</h2>
  <p>
    The sites are delivered through content-delivery and hosting infrastructure that may,
    as a matter of normal operation, keep short-lived technical logs (such as request
    counts or error records). These logs are used to keep the sites available and are not
    used to identify or profile visitors. We do not access such logs for visitor-specific
    purposes.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Email communication</h2>
  <p>
    If you contact us at landengltd@gmail.com, we will use your email address only to
    respond to your message. We do not add correspondents to mailing lists and we do not
    share, sell or rent contact details to anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Pages on both sites link to external resources, such as ctext.org for classical
    source texts. When you follow such a link you leave our sites, and the third party's
    own privacy policy applies. We recommend reviewing it.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Data security and retention</h2>
  <p>
    Because we do not collect personal data through the sites, there is no visitor data
    stored on our systems to secure or delete. Correspondence we receive by email is
    retained only as long as needed to handle the matter.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Children</h2>
  <p>
    The sites are general educational publications not directed at children. Because we
    collect no personal data, no child-specific data processing can occur on our side.
  </p>

  <h2>9. International visitors</h2>
  <p>
    The sites may be accessed worldwide. No personal data is transferred because no
    personal data is collected; where hosting infrastructure caches content, such caching
    contains no information about you.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If we ever introduce a feature that changes this position (for example, a newsletter),
    this policy will be updated first and the change dated. The current version is always
    the one published at this address.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Privacy questions: Martin.W &middot; Phone / WhatsApp: +86 13323237275 &middot;
    Email: landengltd@gmail.com
  </p>
</Base>
